 "notes": "Statement: Luogu P8291 ([\u7701\u9009\u8054\u8003 2022] \u5b66\u672f\u793e\u533a, the DMOJ page is behind a challenge). No accepted C++ (every submission is TLE or RTE), so orig.cpp is a corpus-written reference: mutual (a b loushang)(b a louxia) pairs first, then a Dinic matching of next slots to previous slots through per-person hubs, then each matching cycle (all louxia or all loushang) is broken by a swap with the poster's academic message. Orders are not unique, so checker.py checks the count against the answer and replays the order. Its counts match the m <= 16 bitmask DP in 4533926 on 400 generated cases."
